.el .ds Aq '
.TH tissue 1  "tissue 0.1.10" 
.SH NAME
tissue \- Tissue command\-line interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtissue\fR [\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Tissue — issue tracker for development with AI in the loop.
.PP
Every unit of work lives in a plain git repo as files: a human format (`issue.md`) owned by humans, and an AI format (`agent.jsonl`) owned by agents. This CLI is the local interface to both.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Path to the tissue repository (directory containing `.tissue/`). Defaults to the current directory
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
tissue\-init(1)
Initialize a tissue repository: create the `.tissue/` structure, optionally configuring a remote and importing GitHub issues (#37)
.TP
tissue\-create(1)
Create a new issue
.TP
tissue\-list(1)
List issues; issues awaiting a human decision are flagged `[awaiting decision]` (stored tag: `needs\-review`)
.TP
tissue\-show(1)
Print one issue: front matter fields and body
.TP
tissue\-sync(1)
Record a human edit in the AI stream: agents reconcile from this record onward, never from raw diffs. Run after editing issue.md
.TP
tissue\-propose(1)
Propose a change to an issue\*(Aqs human format for review. Fails safe if the current value no longer matches
.TP
tissue\-approve(1)
Approve a pending proposal: applies the edit and clears `needs\-review`
.TP
tissue\-serve(1)
Serve the read\-only local viewer (GUI) on 127.0.0.1. Loopback\-only; no remote exposure
.TP
tissue\-pull(1)
Fetch the remote and rebase onto it — never a merge commit (#110). On conflict: aborts, names the affected issue ids
.TP
tissue\-push(1)
Push to the remote: fast\-forward only, or `\-\-force\-with\-lease` after a pull\-rebase (#110). Refuses anything else
.TP
tissue\-reject(1)
Reject a pending proposal: records the reason so agents can learn from it, and clears `needs\-review`
.TP
tissue\-release(1)
Release subcommands: create / list / show / assign / cut
.TP
tissue\-project(1)
Project subcommands: add / list / remove (#119)
.TP
tissue\-token(1)
API token subcommands: issue / list / revoke (#159). Secrets are stored as SHA\-256 hashes only — the plaintext is printed once
.TP
tissue\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.1.10
